   '[{"id":"a","text":"Application filing, site validation, preparation of a Community Resource Management Framework (CRMF), approval by DENR"},{"id":"b","text":"Preparation of a Community Resource Management Framework (CRMF), application filing, site validation, approval by DENR"},{"id":"c","text":"Site validation, application filing, preparation of a Community Resource Management Framework (CRMF), approval by DENR"},{"id":"d","text":"Application filing, preparation of a Community Resource Management Framework (CRMF), site validation, approval by DENR"}]'::jsonb, 'a'),
  ('fg-g00135', 'forest-governance', 'policy-and-administration', 'Hard', 'practice',
   'Under the Philippine Forestry Laws, what is the primary distinction between a Forest Land Use Plan (FLUP) and a Comprehensive Land Use Plan (CLUP)?',
   '[{"id":"a","text":"FLUP is prepared by the DENR, while CLUP is prepared by the Department of Agriculture."},{"id":"b","text":"FLUP focuses on agricultural land use, while CLUP is for urban development only."},{"id":"c","text":"FLUP is specifically for forest lands, while CLUP encompasses all land types within a municipality."},{"id":"d","text":"FLUP and CLUP are synonymous, with no distinct differences."}]'::jsonb, 'c'),
  ('fg-g00136', 'forest-governance', 'policy-and-administration', 'Hard', 'practice',
   'What policy mechanism under the Philippine forestry law is designed to facilitate conflict resolution among stakeholders involved in the management of community-based forest resources?',
   '[{"id":"a","text":"Comprehensive Agrarian Reform Program (CARP)"},{"id":"b","text":"Protected Area Management Board (PAMB)"},{"id":"c","text":"Environmental Impact Assessment (EIA)"},{"id":"d","text":"Multi-Sectoral Forest Protection Committees (MFPCs)"}]'::jsonb, 'd'),
  ('fg-g00137', 'forest-governance', 'policy-and-administration', 'Hard', 'practice',
   'According to Philippine forestry policies, what is the purpose of a protected area sustainability funding mechanism established under the Expanded NIPAS Act?',
   '[{"id":"a","text":"To ensure long-term financial support for the management of protected areas."},{"id":"b","text":"To provide immediate financial assistance during natural disasters."},{"id":"c","text":"To fund community infrastructure projects in adjacent areas."},{"id":"d","text":"To subsidize agricultural practices within protected areas."}]'::jsonb, 'a'),
  ('fg-g00138', 'forest-governance', 'policy-and-administration', 'Hard', 'practice',
   'Which provision of the Indigenous Peoples'' Rights Act (IPRA) primarily ensures that the plans and projects in ancestral domains reflect the aspirations and welfare of indigenous communities?',
   '[{"id":"a","text":"Ancestral Domain Sustainable Development and Protection Plan (ADSDPP)"},{"id":"b","text":"Free and Prior Informed Consent (FPIC)"},{"id":"c","text":"Certificate of Ancestral Land Title (CALT)"},{"id":"d","text":"Certificate of Ancestral Domain Title (CADT)"}]'::jsonb, 'a'),
  ('fg-g00139', 'forest-governance', 'policy-and-administration', 'Hard', 'practice',
   'In a CBFMA, what is the primary legal obligation of the holder regarding environmental compliance, according to Philippine forestry regulations?',
   '[{"id":"a","text":"Submit an Environmental Impact Statement (EIS) every five years."},{"id":"b","text":"Conduct annual reforestation activities."},{"id":"c","text":"Report bi-annual profit and loss statements to the DENR."},{"id":"d","text":"Ensure compliance with the Environmental Compliance Certificate (ECC) requirements."}]'::jsonb, 'd'),
  ('fg-g00140', 'forest-governance', 'policy-and-administration', 'Hard', 'practice',
   'Which Philippine forestry policy outlines the process and requirements for obtaining an Environmental Compliance Certificate (ECC) for projects within forest lands?',
   '[{"id":"a","text":"Presidential Decree No. 705, Revised Forestry Code"},{"id":"b","text":"Republic Act No. 9147, Wildlife Resources Conservation and Protection Act"},{"id":"c","text":"Republic Act No. 7586, NIPAS Act"},{"id":"d","text":"Presidential Decree No. 1586, Environmental Impact Statement System"}]'::jsonb, 'd'),
  ('fg-g00141', 'forest-governance', 'policy-and-administration', 'Hard', 'practice',
   'Within the context of Philippine forestry governance, which entity is primarily responsible for the formulation and implementation of forest policies at the national level?',
   '[{"id":"a","text":"Department of Environment and Natural Resources (DENR)"},{"id":"b","text":"National Commission on Indigenous Peoples (NCIP)"},{"id":"c","text":"Local Government Units (LGUs)"},{"id":"d","text":"Bureau of Fisheries and Aquatic Resources (BFAR)"}]'::jsonb, 'a'),
  ('fg-g00142', 'forest-governance', 'policy-and-administration', 'Hard', 'practice',
   'What is the primary objective of establishing Barangay Forest Protection and Management Councils (BFPMC) under the Community-Based Forest Management Strategy in the Philippines?',
   '[{"id":"a","text":"To centralize forest management practices at the national level."},{"id":"b","text":"To replace the role of the DENR in managing protected areas."},{"id":"c","text":"To engage local communities in forest protection and sustainable management."},{"id":"d","text":"To promote urban development within forest lands."}]'::jsonb, 'c'),
  ('fg-g00143', 'forest-governance', 'policy-and-administration', 'Hard', 'practice',
   'Under Republic Act No. 11038, the Expanded National Integrated Protected Areas System (E-NIPAS) Act, what is the significance of the ''Protected Area Management Effectiveness Tracking Tool'' (PA-METT)?',
   '[{"id":"a","text":"It is a tool for assessing the effectiveness of management practices in protected areas."},{"id":"b","text":"It is used to monitor the financial transactions within protected areas."},{"id":"c","text":"It serves as a guideline for the reclassification of protected areas."},{"id":"d","text":"It provides a legal framework for resolving land disputes within protected areas."}]'::jsonb, 'a'),
  ('fg-g00144', 'forest-governance', 'policy-and-administration', 'Hard', 'practice',
   'What is the primary distinction between a Certificate of Ancestral Domain Title (CADT) and a Certificate of Ancestral Land Title (CALT) under the Indigenous Peoples'' Rights Act (IPRA)?',
   '[{"id":"a","text":"CADT pertains to private land ownership while CALT pertains to public land."},{"id":"b","text":"CADT is issued by the DENR, while CALT is issued by the Department of Agrarian Reform."},{"id":"c","text":"There is no legal distinction between CADT and CALT under IPRA."},{"id":"d","text":"CADT covers an entire ancestral domain, whereas CALT is for specific parcels of ancestral land."}]'::jsonb, 'd'),
  ('fg-g00145', 'forest-governance', 'policy-and-administration', 'Hard', 'practice',
   'In the context of the Philippine Forest Management Strategy, what is the primary role of the Forest Land Use Plan (FLUP)?',
   '[{"id":"a","text":"To allocate financial resources for forest conservation projects."},{"id":"b","text":"To facilitate the establishment of new national parks."},{"id":"c","text":"To serve as a blueprint for urban development within forest regions."},{"id":"d","text":"To ensure that land use within forestlands is sustainable and in accordance with national priorities."}]'::jsonb, 'd'),
  ('fg-g00146', 'forest-governance', 'policy-and-administration', 'Hard', 'practice',
   'Under the Indigenous Peoples'' Rights Act (IPRA), what is the primary purpose of the Ancestral Domains Management Plan (ADMP)?',
   '[{"id":"a","text":"To establish zoning regulations within ancestral domains."},{"id":"b","text":"To identify mineral resources for extraction within ancestral domains."},{"id":"c","text":"To outline the management and utilization of ancestral lands by indigenous communities."},{"id":"d","text":"To designate areas within ancestral lands for commercial tourism development."}]'::jsonb, 'c'),
  ('fg-g00147', 'forest-governance', 'policy-and-administration', 'Hard', 'practice',
   'According to Philippine forestry law, how does the Community-Based Forest Management Agreement (CBFMA) differ from the Socialized Industrial Forest Management Agreement (SIFMA)?',
   '[{"id":"a","text":"CBFMA is granted to individuals while SIFMA is granted to communities."},{"id":"b","text":"CBFMA focuses on sustainable livelihood for communities, while SIFMA focuses on industrial use of forest resources."},{"id":"c","text":"CBFMA allows commercial logging, whereas SIFMA strictly prohibits it."},{"id":"d","text":"CBFMA is limited to upland areas, while SIFMA applies to all types of forestlands."}]'::jsonb, 'b'),
  ('fg-g00148', 'forest-governance', 'policy-and-administration', 'Hard', 'practice',
   'What is the main administrative function of the Department of Environment and Natural Resources (DENR) in relation to the implementation of the National Integrated Protected Areas System (NIPAS) Act?',
   '[{"id":"a","text":"To oversee the commercial development of protected areas."},{"id":"b","text":"To issue permits for mining activities within protected areas."},{"id":"c","text":"To manage and supervise the implementation of policies for the conservation of biodiversity in protected areas."},{"id":"d","text":"To facilitate international trade agreements related to forest products."}]'::jsonb, 'c'),
  ('fg-g00149', 'forest-governance', 'policy-and-administration', 'Hard', 'practice',
   'Under the Revised Forestry Code of the Philippines (PD 705), what is the primary purpose of designating buffer zones within forest reserves?',
   '[{"id":"a","text":"To allow for the construction of resort facilities."},{"id":"b","text":"To expand agricultural activities adjacent to forest reserves."},{"id":"c","text":"To create zones for high-density residential development."},{"id":"d","text":"To serve as a transition area between different land uses, minimizing negative impacts on forest ecosystems."}]'::jsonb, 'd'),
