  ('fg-g00295', 'forest-governance', 'forest-protection', 'Hard', 'practice',
   'What is the role of the Indigenous Peoples'' Rights Act (RA 8371) in the context of forest protection and conservation?',
   '[{"id":"a","text":"RA 8371 restricts indigenous peoples from entering forested areas to minimize human impact."},{"id":"b","text":"RA 8371 encourages the displacement of indigenous communities for better forest management."},{"id":"c","text":"RA 8371 recognizes the rights of indigenous peoples to manage and protect their ancestral domains, including forests."},{"id":"d","text":"RA 8371 focuses solely on promoting indigenous culture and has no provisions for forest protection."}]'::jsonb, 'c'),
  ('fg-g00296', 'forest-governance', 'forest-protection', 'Hard', 'practice',
   'In the management of forest reserves, how does the Revised Forestry Code of the Philippines facilitate forest protection regarding forest land use planning?',
   '[{"id":"a","text":"By allowing unrestricted development and conversion of forest lands for commercial purposes."},{"id":"b","text":"By prohibiting any form of land use planning to preserve natural conditions."},{"id":"c","text":"By mandating the preparation of a comprehensive land use plan that includes forest protection measures."},{"id":"d","text":"By delegating all land use planning responsibilities solely to private entities."}]'::jsonb, 'c'),
  ('fg-g00297', 'forest-governance', 'forest-protection', 'Hard', 'practice',
   'What strategy does RA 9147 employ to protect forests from illegal exploitation of wildlife?',
   '[{"id":"a","text":"RA 9147 promotes the legal trade of all wildlife species."},{"id":"b","text":"RA 9147 provides financial incentives for capturing wildlife."},{"id":"c","text":"RA 9147 creates a registry for domesticated wildlife species."},{"id":"d","text":"RA 9147 establishes wildlife trafficking reporting hotlines."}]'::jsonb, 'd'),
  ('fg-g00298', 'forest-governance', 'forest-protection', 'Hard', 'practice',
   'In the context of forest protection, what is the significance of establishing co-management agreements between the DENR and local government units (LGUs)?',
   '[{"id":"a","text":"Co-management agreements allow for the sale of forest products without restrictions."},{"id":"b","text":"They transfer all forest management responsibilities to the LGUs without DENR oversight."},{"id":"c","text":"They enable joint efforts in forest protection, enhancing resource allocation and community involvement."},{"id":"d","text":"Co-management agreements focus solely on commercial logging operations."}]'::jsonb, 'c'),
  ('fg-g00299', 'forest-governance', 'forest-protection', 'Hard', 'practice',
   'How does RA 7586, the National Integrated Protected Areas System (NIPAS) Act, contribute to forest protection through the establishment of Protected Area Management Boards (PAMB)?',
   '[{"id":"a","text":"PAMB allows unrestricted access to all areas within a protected area."},{"id":"b","text":"PAMB focuses exclusively on tourism development within protected areas."},{"id":"c","text":"PAMB is primarily concerned with the commercial exploitation of the protected area''s resources."},{"id":"d","text":"PAMB is responsible for enforcing laws and regulations aimed at protecting the biodiversity of the protected area."}]'::jsonb, 'd'),
  ('fg-g00300', 'forest-governance', 'forest-protection', 'Hard', 'practice',
   'What specific action does PD 705 authorize the DENR to take in order to prevent forest fires?',
   '[{"id":"a","text":"DENR is authorized to conduct controlled burning in all forest areas indiscriminately."},{"id":"b","text":"DENR is responsible for the promotion of firewood collection as a preventive measure against forest fires."},{"id":"c","text":"DENR is authorized to stop any form of human activity in forests during dry seasons."},{"id":"d","text":"DENR can establish and maintain an efficient fire protection organization in every forest district."}]'::jsonb, 'd'),
  ('fg-g00301', 'forest-governance', 'forest-protection', 'Hard', 'practice',
   'What is a key distinction between RA 9147 and RA 7586 in terms of forest protection emphasis?',
   '[{"id":"a","text":"RA 9147 focuses on the management of mining activities, whereas RA 7586 deals with urban development in forests."},{"id":"b","text":"RA 9147 prioritizes commercial forestry, while RA 7586 emphasizes recreational use of forests."},{"id":"c","text":"RA 9147 emphasizes wildlife conservation, while RA 7586 focuses on the protection of diverse ecosystems within protected areas."},{"id":"d","text":"RA 9147 targets marine conservation, whereas RA 7586 is concerned with terrestrial habitats."}]'::jsonb, 'c'),
  ('fg-g00302', 'forest-governance', 'forest-protection', 'Hard', 'practice',
   'What is the primary purpose of establishing fire lookouts in forest protection?',
   '[{"id":"a","text":"To monitor wildlife populations."},{"id":"b","text":"To provide early detection of forest fire outbreaks."},{"id":"c","text":"To assess forest regeneration rates."},{"id":"d","text":"To estimate timber stock."}]'::jsonb, 'b'),
  ('fg-g00303', 'forest-governance', 'forest-protection', 'Hard', 'practice',
   'Under the Revised Forestry Code of the Philippines (PD 705), how are forest protection activities funded?',
   '[{"id":"a","text":"Through international loans and grants specifically for reforestation."},{"id":"b","text":"Through government budget allocations in the annual General Appropriations Act."},{"id":"c","text":"By imposing fines collected from illegal logging activities."},{"id":"d","text":"Through local government unit (LGU) contributions."}]'::jsonb, 'b'),
  ('fg-g00304', 'forest-governance', 'forest-protection', 'Hard', 'practice',
   'What is a critical component of implementing forest protection measures under RA 7586 (NIPAS) regarding the management of protected areas?',
   '[{"id":"a","text":"Setting up commercial logging operations within protected areas."},{"id":"b","text":"Establishing a Protected Area Management Board (PAMB) for each site."},{"id":"c","text":"Promoting tourism development without restriction."},{"id":"d","text":"Allowing unrestricted agricultural expansion."}]'::jsonb, 'b'),
  ('fg-g00305', 'forest-governance', 'forest-protection', 'Hard', 'practice',
   'How does the Community-Based Forest Management Agreement (CBFMA) enhance forest protection efforts in the Philippines?',
   '[{"id":"a","text":"By granting exclusive land ownership to private companies."},{"id":"b","text":"By encouraging urban development in forest lands."},{"id":"c","text":"Through joint forest management between communities and DENR."},{"id":"d","text":"Through the imposition of high tariffs on wood exports."}]'::jsonb, 'c'),
  ('fg-g00306', 'forest-governance', 'forest-protection', 'Hard', 'practice',
   'In forest protection, what role does the establishment of community-based fire management teams play?',
   '[{"id":"a","text":"To exclusively handle agricultural burning permits."},{"id":"b","text":"To facilitate the sale of firewood to local markets."},{"id":"c","text":"To promote the use of fire in land clearing."},{"id":"d","text":"To increase community awareness and participation in forest fire prevention."}]'::jsonb, 'd'),
  ('fg-g00307', 'forest-governance', 'forest-protection', 'Hard', 'practice',
   'Which is a primary focus of the Indigenous Peoples'' Rights Act (RA 8371) in relation to forest protection?',
   '[{"id":"a","text":"Promoting large-scale mining activities in ancestral domains."},{"id":"b","text":"Encouraging the privatization of communal forests."},{"id":"c","text":"Allowing uncontrolled logging in indigenous territories."},{"id":"d","text":"Recognizing and respecting the rights of indigenous communities over their ancestral lands."}]'::jsonb, 'd'),
  ('fg-g00308', 'forest-governance', 'forest-protection', 'Hard', 'practice',
   'What is the significance of establishing a forest protection committee under the Local Government Code of the Philippines?',
   '[{"id":"a","text":"To facilitate coordination between local communities and national agencies in forest protection efforts."},{"id":"b","text":"To centralize all forest management decisions at the national level."},{"id":"c","text":"To prioritize commercial logging within municipal boundaries."},{"id":"d","text":"To restrict community involvement in forest protection activities."}]'::jsonb, 'a'),
  ('fg-g00309', 'forest-governance', 'forest-protection', 'Hard', 'practice',
   'How does RA 9147, the Wildlife Resources Conservation and Protection Act, support forest protection?',
   '[{"id":"a","text":"By promoting infrastructure development in forest areas."},{"id":"b","text":"By issuing permits for mining activities in protected forests."},{"id":"c","text":"By encouraging agricultural expansion into wildlife habitats."},{"id":"d","text":"By regulating the hunting and collection of wildlife to maintain ecological balance."}]'::jsonb, 'd'),
  ('fg-g00310', 'forest-governance', 'forest-protection', 'Hard', 'practice',
   'What is a distinguishing feature of the forest protection strategy under the Expanded NIPAS Act (RA 11038) compared to the original NIPAS Act (RA 7586)?',
   '[{"id":"a","text":"Focus solely on marine ecosystems protection."},{"id":"b","text":"Inclusion of more areas under protection and stricter penalties for violations."},{"id":"c","text":"Removal of community involvement in management decisions."},{"id":"d","text":"Elimination of buffer zones in protected areas."}]'::jsonb, 'b'),
  ('fg-g00311', 'forest-governance', 'forest-protection', 'Hard', 'practice',
   'Under PD 705, what is one action authorized for forest protection officers to prevent illegal logging?',
   '[{"id":"a","text":"Confiscation of equipment and logs found in illegal logging sites."},{"id":"b","text":"Issuing permits for selective logging within protected areas."},{"id":"c","text":"Promoting the sale of confiscated timber to local markets."},{"id":"d","text":"Allowing timber harvesting without restriction in forest reserves."}]'::jsonb, 'a'),
  ('fg-g00312', 'forest-governance', 'forest-protection', 'Hard', 'practice',
   'Under the Revised Forestry Code of the Philippines (PD 705), what is the procedure for apprehending individuals involved in illegal logging activities, and how does it contribute to forest protection?',
   '[{"id":"a","text":"Forest protection officers must gather substantial evidence and file reports to local authorities before making any arrests, ensuring due process and legal compliance."},{"id":"b","text":"Only the police have the authority to apprehend individuals involved in illegal logging, requiring forest protection officers to act as liaisons and report activities."},{"id":"c","text":"Apprehensions are conducted through joint operations with military personnel, ensuring safety and compliance with national security protocols."},{"id":"d","text":"Forest protection officers can immediately apprehend individuals caught in the act of illegal logging, empowering on-site enforcement to prevent further forest degradation."}]'::jsonb, 'd'),
  ('fg-g00313', 'forest-governance', 'environment-sustainable-development', 'Easy', 'practice',
   'What is the main purpose of the National Integrated Protected Areas System (NIPAS) Act of 1992, RA 7586?',
   '[{"id":"a","text":"To establish a comprehensive system of integrated protected areas in the Philippines to conserve biodiversity."},{"id":"b","text":"To promote the industrial use of forest resources in protected areas."},{"id":"c","text":"To encourage the clearing of forests for agricultural expansion."},{"id":"d","text":"To allow unrestricted access to forest resources for commercial purposes."}]'::jsonb, 'a'),
  ('fg-g00314', 'forest-governance', 'environment-sustainable-development', 'Easy', 'practice',
   'Which Philippine law recognizes the rights of Indigenous Peoples to their ancestral domains and integrates their rights into national development plans?',
   '[{"id":"a","text":"RA 8371, known as the Indigenous Peoples'' Rights Act (IPRA)."},{"id":"b","text":"RA 7586, National Integrated Protected Areas System Act."},{"id":"c","text":"PD 705, the Revised Forestry Code."},{"id":"d","text":"RA 9147, the Wildlife Resources Conservation and Protection Act."}]'::jsonb, 'a'),
  ('fg-g00315', 'forest-governance', 'environment-sustainable-development', 'Easy', 'practice',
   'The process of granting tenure to forest occupants and communities to promote sustainable forest management is known as:',
   '[{"id":"a","text":"Industrial Reforestation."},{"id":"b","text":"Community-Based Forest Management (CBFM)."},{"id":"c","text":"Illegal Logging Amnesty."},{"id":"d","text":"Forest Exploitation Licensing."}]'::jsonb, 'b'),
  ('fg-g00316', 'forest-governance', 'environment-sustainable-development', 'Easy', 'practice',
