   '[{"id":"a","text":"To encourage agricultural expansion and increase food production."},{"id":"b","text":"To serve as sites for commercial mining activities."},{"id":"c","text":"To provide a transitional area that reduces human impact on core conservation zones."},{"id":"d","text":"To limit access to local communities entirely."}]'::jsonb, 'c'),
  ('fg-g00377', 'forest-governance', 'environment-sustainable-development', 'Hard', 'practice',
   'Which aspect of Republic Act 8371, the Indigenous Peoples'' Rights Act (IPRA), directly supports sustainable development in forest management in the Philippines?',
   '[{"id":"a","text":"Commercial exploitation of forest resources by foreign entities."},{"id":"b","text":"Centralized governmental control over all forest management decisions."},{"id":"c","text":"Recognition and respect for Indigenous Peoples'' ancestral lands and traditional practices."},{"id":"d","text":"Prioritization of infrastructure development over conservation efforts."}]'::jsonb, 'c'),
  ('fg-g00378', 'forest-governance', 'environment-sustainable-development', 'Hard', 'practice',
   'Under the provisions for sustainable development, how does Enhanced National Greening Program (E-NGP) address climate change mitigation in the Philippines?',
   '[{"id":"a","text":"By increasing the rate of deforestation to provide land for urban development."},{"id":"b","text":"By promoting the planting of monoculture plantations of fast-growing species."},{"id":"c","text":"By enhancing carbon sequestration through large-scale reforestation with diverse native species."},{"id":"d","text":"By focusing on the elimination of indigenous species to prevent competition."}]'::jsonb, 'c'),
  ('fg-g00379', 'forest-governance', 'environment-sustainable-development', 'Hard', 'practice',
   'What role does Republic Act 7586, as amended by RA 11038, play in ensuring sustainable development in the management of protected areas in the Philippines?',
   '[{"id":"a","text":"It mandates the conversion of protected areas into industrial zones."},{"id":"b","text":"It allows for unrestricted access and resource extraction within protected areas."},{"id":"c","text":"It ensures the integration of biodiversity conservation with sustainable livelihood programs for local communities."},{"id":"d","text":"It focuses solely on marine ecosystems, ignoring terrestrial protected areas."}]'::jsonb, 'c'),
  ('fg-g00380', 'forest-governance', 'environment-sustainable-development', 'Hard', 'practice',
   'How does the concept of Payment for Ecosystem Services (PES) contribute to sustainable forest management in the Philippines?',
   '[{"id":"a","text":"By allowing large corporations to bypass environmental regulations through financial compensation."},{"id":"b","text":"By mandating that all ecosystem services be provided for free by local communities."},{"id":"c","text":"By providing economic incentives to landowners and communities to maintain and enhance ecosystem services."},{"id":"d","text":"By focusing solely on the conservation of water resources, ignoring other ecosystem services."}]'::jsonb, 'c'),
  ('fg-g00381', 'forest-governance', 'environment-sustainable-development', 'Hard', 'practice',
   'In the framework of sustainable forest management in the Philippines, what is a significant benefit of implementing Community-Based Forest Management Agreements (CBFMA)?',
   '[{"id":"a","text":"Centralizing forest management under government control to ensure uniform policies."},{"id":"b","text":"Empowering local communities to manage forest resources, which can enhance stewardship and sustainability."},{"id":"c","text":"Focusing on short-term profits from large-scale commercial logging activities."},{"id":"d","text":"Promoting deforestation to make way for agricultural expansion."}]'::jsonb, 'b'),
  ('fg-g00382', 'forest-governance', 'environment-sustainable-development', 'Hard', 'practice',
   'What is a primary environmental objective of Reduced Impact Logging (RIL) techniques in the context of sustainable forestry in the Philippines?',
   '[{"id":"a","text":"To maximize timber yield regardless of environmental impacts."},{"id":"b","text":"To minimize damage to surrounding forest ecosystems and maintain biodiversity."},{"id":"c","text":"To accelerate the removal of all non-commercial tree species."},{"id":"d","text":"To encourage the use of heavy machinery for faster logging operations."}]'::jsonb, 'b'),
  ('fg-g00383', 'forest-governance', 'environment-sustainable-development', 'Hard', 'practice',
   'How does Republic Act 9147, the Wildlife Resources Conservation and Protection Act, aim to support sustainable development within forest ecosystems in the Philippines?',
   '[{"id":"a","text":"By promoting the trade and consumption of endangered species."},{"id":"b","text":"By encouraging the introduction of non-native species to enhance biodiversity."},{"id":"c","text":"By establishing legal frameworks for the conservation and protection of wildlife resources."},{"id":"d","text":"By focusing exclusively on terrestrial wildlife, ignoring aquatic ecosystems."}]'::jsonb, 'c'),
  ('fg-g00384', 'forest-governance', 'environment-sustainable-development', 'Hard', 'practice',
   'In the context of Philippine forest governance, what is a critical strategy under sustainable development for maintaining ecological balance while supporting economic activities?',
   '[{"id":"a","text":"Exclusive reliance on extractive industries for economic growth."},{"id":"b","text":"Complete conversion of natural forests into plantations for economic purposes."},{"id":"c","text":"Integration of sustainable livelihood projects with conservation efforts to support local communities."},{"id":"d","text":"Implementation of strict bans on all types of forest use."}]'::jsonb, 'c'),
  ('fg-g00385', 'forest-governance', 'environment-sustainable-development', 'Hard', 'practice',
   'Under the National Integrated Protected Areas System (NIPAS) Act, how is the concept of ''zoning'' used to promote sustainable development within protected areas in the Philippines?',
   '[{"id":"a","text":"By designating zones for tourism, agriculture, and urban development indiscriminately."},{"id":"b","text":"By allowing unrestricted resource extraction in core zones to support local economies."},{"id":"c","text":"By creating buffer zones that prioritize infrastructure development over conservation."},{"id":"d","text":"By separating areas for strict protection, sustainable use, and restoration to balance conservation and development."}]'::jsonb, 'd'),
  ('fg-g00386', 'forest-governance', 'environment-sustainable-development', 'Hard', 'practice',
   'How does the Community-Based Forest Management Agreement (CBFMA) align with sustainable development goals in the Philippines?',
   '[{"id":"a","text":"By encouraging commercial logging without any community involvement."},{"id":"b","text":"By excluding indigenous peoples from decision-making processes related to forest management."},{"id":"c","text":"By prioritizing industrial plantations over biodiversity conservation."},{"id":"d","text":"By involving local communities in the management and use of forest resources, thereby enhancing their livelihoods and forest conservation."}]'::jsonb, 'd'),
  ('fg-g00387', 'forest-governance', 'environment-sustainable-development', 'Hard', 'practice',
   'In the context of environment and sustainable development, how does the concept of ''ecosystem services'' support forest management in the Philippines?',
   '[{"id":"a","text":"By recognizing and valuing the multiple benefits forests provide, such as water regulation, carbon sequestration, and biodiversity, encouraging sustainable management practices."},{"id":"b","text":"By promoting the idea that forests only provide timber and no other benefits."},{"id":"c","text":"By focusing solely on aesthetic values of forests, ignoring ecological functions."},{"id":"d","text":"By disregarding the social and cultural values of forests to local communities."}]'::jsonb, 'a'),
  ('fg-g00388', 'forest-governance', 'environment-sustainable-development', 'Hard', 'practice',
   'What mechanism does Republic Act 11038, the Expanded National Integrated Protected Areas System (E-NIPAS) Act, introduce to enhance sustainable development within protected areas?',
   '[{"id":"a","text":"It introduces the concept of management plans with community participation, integrating conservation with local development needs."},{"id":"b","text":"It removes legal protections from all protected areas to stimulate economic growth."},{"id":"c","text":"It allows complete privatization of protected areas for exclusive commercial use."},{"id":"d","text":"It prohibits any form of tourism and recreation in all protected areas."}]'::jsonb, 'a'),
  ('fg-g00389', 'forest-governance', 'environment-sustainable-development', 'Hard', 'practice',
   'In sustainable development, what is the role of ''adaptive management'' in forest ecosystems in the Philippines?',
   '[{"id":"a","text":"To allow flexibility in management plans, enabling adjustments based on monitoring and changing environmental and social conditions."},{"id":"b","text":"To maintain static management plans that are not subject to change or adjustment."},{"id":"c","text":"To implement fixed logging schedules without consideration for ecological changes."},{"id":"d","text":"To eliminate community involvement in forest management planning."}]'::jsonb, 'a'),
  ('fg-g00390', 'forest-governance', 'environment-sustainable-development', 'Hard', 'practice',
   'How does the concept of ''intergenerational equity'' guide sustainable forest management practices in the Philippines?',
   '[{"id":"a","text":"By focusing solely on maximizing current economic benefits from forest resources."},{"id":"b","text":"By prioritizing urban development over forest conservation for immediate economic gains."},{"id":"c","text":"By ensuring the conservation of forest resources for future generations while meeting present needs, balancing economic, social, and environmental interests."},{"id":"d","text":"By disregarding the cultural significance of forests to indigenous communities."}]'::jsonb, 'c'),
  ('fg-g00391', 'forest-governance', 'professional-ethics', 'Easy', 'practice',
   'What is the primary purpose of the Code of Ethics for Filipino Foresters?',
   '[{"id":"a","text":"To provide guidelines for ethical conduct and professionalism."},{"id":"b","text":"To outline professional competencies required for foresters."},{"id":"c","text":"To establish salary grades for forestry positions."},{"id":"d","text":"To define the forestry curriculum in universities."}]'::jsonb, 'a'),
  ('fg-g00392', 'forest-governance', 'professional-ethics', 'Easy', 'practice',
   'Which Philippine law governs the professional practice of forestry in the Philippines?',
   '[{"id":"a","text":"RA 7586"},{"id":"b","text":"RA 11038"},{"id":"c","text":"RA 10176"},{"id":"d","text":"RA 6239"}]'::jsonb, 'd'),
  ('fg-g00393', 'forest-governance', 'professional-ethics', 'Easy', 'practice',
   'What is a key value emphasized in the professional ethics of foresters?',
   '[{"id":"a","text":"Profit maximization"},{"id":"b","text":"Rapid deforestation"},{"id":"c","text":"Sustainable resource management"},{"id":"d","text":"Urban development"}]'::jsonb, 'c'),
  ('fg-g00394', 'forest-governance', 'professional-ethics', 'Easy', 'practice',
   'Under the Code of Ethics for Filipino Foresters, which of the following is expected from a professional forester in relation to the environment?',
   '[{"id":"a","text":"To promote conservation and sustainable use of forest resources."},{"id":"b","text":"To prioritize economic interests over environmental concerns."},{"id":"c","text":"To exclusively focus on timber production."},{"id":"d","text":"To ignore the impact of forestry activities on wildlife."}]'::jsonb, 'a'),
  ('fg-g00395', 'forest-governance', 'professional-ethics', 'Easy', 'practice',
   'In professional ethics, what does the principle of ''integrity'' ensure for forestry professionals?',
   '[{"id":"a","text":"Maintaining secrecy about illegal activities."},{"id":"b","text":"Ensuring maximum profits in forestry operations."},{"id":"c","text":"Upholding honesty and moral principles in all professional dealings."},{"id":"d","text":"Focusing on rapid project completion over quality."}]'::jsonb, 'c'),
  ('fg-g00396', 'forest-governance', 'professional-ethics', 'Easy', 'practice',
   'Which body is responsible for enforcing the Code of Ethics for Filipino Foresters?',
