  ('fg-g00436', 'forest-governance', 'professional-ethics', 'Medium', 'practice',
   'According to professional ethics, what is the appropriate response when a forester discovers illegal logging in their area of responsibility?',
   '[{"id":"a","text":"Ignore the activity to avoid conflict"},{"id":"b","text":"Attempt to confront the loggers personally"},{"id":"c","text":"Document the activity without taking further action"},{"id":"d","text":"Report the activity to the appropriate authorities"}]'::jsonb, 'd'),
  ('fg-g00437', 'forest-governance', 'professional-ethics', 'Medium', 'practice',
   'In the context of professional ethics, what is the primary consideration when a forester engages with indigenous communities?',
   '[{"id":"a","text":"Ensuring the forester''s own objectives are met"},{"id":"b","text":"Respecting and prioritizing the rights and traditions of the communities"},{"id":"c","text":"Maximizing the economic benefit of forest resources"},{"id":"d","text":"Maintaining a strict schedule without involving the community"}]'::jsonb, 'b'),
  ('fg-g00438', 'forest-governance', 'professional-ethics', 'Medium', 'practice',
   'Which ethical principle should guide a forester when balancing economic interests with environmental sustainability?',
   '[{"id":"a","text":"Prioritize short-term economic gains"},{"id":"b","text":"Maximize resource extraction for profit"},{"id":"c","text":"Ensure long-term sustainability and ecological integrity"},{"id":"d","text":"Focus solely on industry stakeholder demands"}]'::jsonb, 'c'),
  ('fg-g00439', 'forest-governance', 'professional-ethics', 'Medium', 'practice',
   'What is the ethical responsibility of foresters regarding transparency in reporting forest management activities?',
   '[{"id":"a","text":"Only provide information to those who request it"},{"id":"b","text":"Avoid disclosing any sensitive information under any circumstances"},{"id":"c","text":"Ensure that all reports are accurate, clear, and accessible to stakeholders"},{"id":"d","text":"Report only positive outcomes to maintain public image"}]'::jsonb, 'c'),
  ('fg-g00440', 'forest-governance', 'professional-ethics', 'Medium', 'practice',
   'How should a forester manage receiving gifts from suppliers according to professional ethics?',
   '[{"id":"a","text":"Accept gifts as a sign of goodwill regardless of value"},{"id":"b","text":"Accept gifts and offer preferential treatment"},{"id":"c","text":"Only accept gifts if they are shared with colleagues"},{"id":"d","text":"Politely decline gifts to avoid any potential conflict of interest"}]'::jsonb, 'd'),
  ('fg-g00441', 'forest-governance', 'professional-ethics', 'Medium', 'practice',
   'When a professional forester encounters a situation where forest management decisions could harm biodiversity, what ethical guideline should they follow?',
   '[{"id":"a","text":"Re-evaluate the plan to mitigate potential harm to biodiversity"},{"id":"b","text":"Proceed with the management plan to meet deadlines"},{"id":"c","text":"Ignore the potential impacts on biodiversity"},{"id":"d","text":"Minimize consultation with ecologists to save time"}]'::jsonb, 'a'),
  ('fg-g00442', 'forest-governance', 'professional-ethics', 'Medium', 'practice',
   'In the context of professional ethics, how should foresters handle their own professional development?',
   '[{"id":"a","text":"Rely solely on past education and experience"},{"id":"b","text":"Pursue ongoing education and skills enhancement"},{"id":"c","text":"Focus only on mandatory training provided by employers"},{"id":"d","text":"Ignore professional development to save time"}]'::jsonb, 'b'),
  ('fg-g00443', 'forest-governance', 'professional-ethics', 'Medium', 'practice',
   'What ethical principle should a forester prioritize when conducting environmental impact assessments?',
   '[{"id":"a","text":"Ensuring assessments favor the forester’s employer"},{"id":"b","text":"Only completing assessments if required by law"},{"id":"c","text":"Providing honest, unbiased, and comprehensive assessments"},{"id":"d","text":"Minimizing negative findings to expedite project approval"}]'::jsonb, 'c'),
  ('fg-g00444', 'forest-governance', 'professional-ethics', 'Medium', 'practice',
   'According to professional ethics, how should a forester approach collaborative projects with other professionals?',
   '[{"id":"a","text":"Dominate the project to ensure personal recognition"},{"id":"b","text":"Focus solely on individual contributions without consulting others"},{"id":"c","text":"Work collaboratively while respecting and valuing diverse expertise"},{"id":"d","text":"Avoid collaboration to maintain independence"}]'::jsonb, 'c'),
  ('fg-g00445', 'forest-governance', 'professional-ethics', 'Medium', 'practice',
   'What is a forester’s ethical responsibility when it comes to public education about forest conservation?',
   '[{"id":"a","text":"Only provide information when requested"},{"id":"b","text":"Focus solely on professional duties, leaving education to others"},{"id":"c","text":"Actively engage and inform the public to raise awareness"},{"id":"d","text":"Limit information to technical audiences only"}]'::jsonb, 'c'),
  ('fg-g00446', 'forest-governance', 'professional-ethics', 'Medium', 'practice',
   'In professional ethics, what is the appropriate action for a forester when facing a situation that may compromise their integrity?',
   '[{"id":"a","text":"Prioritize personal gain over professional duties."},{"id":"b","text":"Consult with colleagues and adhere to the code of ethics."},{"id":"c","text":"Ignore the situation and hope for the best outcome."},{"id":"d","text":"Take immediate action based on personal beliefs only."}]'::jsonb, 'b'),
  ('fg-g00447', 'forest-governance', 'professional-ethics', 'Medium', 'practice',
   'When dealing with community stakeholders, which ethical principle should guide a forester’s actions according to professional values?',
   '[{"id":"a","text":"Avoid engaging with community members to maintain objectivity."},{"id":"b","text":"Ensure transparency and respect in all communications."},{"id":"c","text":"Focus solely on the economic benefits of forestry operations."},{"id":"d","text":"Disregard community input if it conflicts with personal opinions."}]'::jsonb, 'b'),
  ('fg-g00448', 'forest-governance', 'professional-ethics', 'Medium', 'practice',
   'According to professional ethics, how should a forester handle a situation where financial incentives are offered in exchange for overlooking environmental regulations?',
   '[{"id":"a","text":"Report the incident to appropriate authorities and refuse the incentives."},{"id":"b","text":"Accept the incentives as a normal part of doing business."},{"id":"c","text":"Negotiate for a higher incentive before making a decision."},{"id":"d","text":"Ignore the offer and continue with current practices."}]'::jsonb, 'a'),
  ('fg-g00449', 'forest-governance', 'professional-ethics', 'Medium', 'practice',
   'Which ethical responsibility should a forester prioritize when conducting research involving indigenous knowledge?',
   '[{"id":"a","text":"Ensure that the research findings are shared with the community."},{"id":"b","text":"Prioritize the forester''s personal research goals over community input."},{"id":"c","text":"Keep all research methods and findings confidential from the community."},{"id":"d","text":"Focus on financial gains from the research above all else."}]'::jsonb, 'a'),
  ('fg-g00450', 'forest-governance', 'professional-ethics', 'Medium', 'practice',
   'How should a forester approach the development of a forest management plan in terms of professional ethics?',
   '[{"id":"a","text":"Develop the plan independently without input from others."},{"id":"b","text":"Consult with stakeholders to incorporate diverse perspectives."},{"id":"c","text":"Only consider economic factors in the management plan."},{"id":"d","text":"Follow outdated practices without considering new information."}]'::jsonb, 'b'),
  ('fg-g00451', 'forest-governance', 'professional-ethics', 'Medium', 'practice',
   'When engaging in professional development, what ethical consideration should guide a forester’s actions?',
   '[{"id":"a","text":"Only participate if there is a direct financial benefit."},{"id":"b","text":"Avoid any development activities to save time."},{"id":"c","text":"Participate only in mandatory sessions without further effort."},{"id":"d","text":"Engage continuously to maintain and enhance professional competence."}]'::jsonb, 'd'),
  ('fg-g00452', 'forest-governance', 'professional-ethics', 'Medium', 'practice',
   'What is the ethical approach for a forester when collaborating with other professionals on a forestry project?',
   '[{"id":"a","text":"Prioritize the forester''s personal goals over the team''s objectives."},{"id":"b","text":"Refuse to collaborate to maintain professional independence."},{"id":"c","text":"Ensure that all collaborators adhere to the highest ethical standards."},{"id":"d","text":"Focus solely on personal recognition for the project''s success."}]'::jsonb, 'c'),
  ('fg-g00453', 'forest-governance', 'professional-ethics', 'Hard', 'practice',
   'Under the Code of Ethics for Filipino foresters, how should a forester ethically approach the reconciliation of conflicting interests between economic development and forest conservation?',
   '[{"id":"a","text":"Prioritize economic development over conservation if it benefits the largest number of people."},{"id":"b","text":"Seek a balanced approach that fulfills legal requirements and ensures sustainable use of resources."},{"id":"c","text":"Advocate solely for forest conservation without regard for economic impacts."},{"id":"d","text":"Make decisions based on personal judgment rather than legal or ethical guidelines."}]'::jsonb, 'b'),
  ('fg-g00454', 'forest-governance', 'professional-ethics', 'Hard', 'practice',
   'What ethical principle should guide a forester''s decision when faced with a potential conflict between government policy and indigenous peoples'' rights?',
   '[{"id":"a","text":"Always follow government policy as it is legally binding."},{"id":"b","text":"Engage in dialogue with both parties to find a compromise that respects indigenous rights and complies with policy."},{"id":"c","text":"Support the indigenous rights if they align with professional values, regardless of policy."},{"id":"d","text":"Ignore the conflict and proceed with government directives."}]'::jsonb, 'b'),
  ('fg-g00455', 'forest-governance', 'professional-ethics', 'Hard', 'practice',
   'In the context of professional ethics, how should foresters manage the confidentiality of traditional ecological knowledge shared by local communities?',
   '[{"id":"a","text":"Incorporate the knowledge into public reports to promote awareness."},{"id":"b","text":"Share it with external researchers for further study."},{"id":"c","text":"Use the knowledge freely as it is not protected by intellectual property laws."},{"id":"d","text":"Obtain explicit consent from the community before using or sharing the knowledge."}]'::jsonb, 'd'),
  ('fg-g00456', 'forest-governance', 'professional-ethics', 'Hard', 'practice',
   'Which ethical consideration should guide a forester in a situation where a project''s environmental assessment reveals significant but legally permissible impacts?',
   '[{"id":"a","text":"Proceed with the project since it complies with the law."},{"id":"b","text":"Advocate for additional mitigations to reduce environmental impact."},{"id":"c","text":"Ignore personal concerns and focus on project completion."},{"id":"d","text":"Postpone the project indefinitely until impacts are eliminated."}]'::jsonb, 'b'),
  ('fg-g00457', 'forest-governance', 'professional-ethics', 'Hard', 'practice',
   'How should a professional forester approach a situation where a new management plan could lead to short-term economic gains but long-term ecological damage?',
   '[{"id":"a","text":"Prioritize short-term economic gains as they provide immediate benefits."},{"id":"b","text":"Focus solely on avoiding ecological damage, ignoring economic aspects."},{"id":"c","text":"Develop a strategy that minimizes ecological damage while considering economic needs."},{"id":"d","text":"Implement the plan as proposed, trusting future solutions will address ecological concerns."}]'::jsonb, 'c'),
  ('fg-g00458', 'forest-governance', 'professional-ethics', 'Hard', 'practice',
   'When engaging with indigenous communities, what ethical obligation does a forester have according to professional ethics?',
   '[{"id":"a","text":"Implement projects based on external best practices without local input."},{"id":"b","text":"Prioritize governmental policies over community preferences."},{"id":"c","text":"Consult with the community and incorporate their input into decision-making processes."},{"id":"d","text":"Avoid engaging with the community to prevent potential conflicts."}]'::jsonb, 'c'),
  ('fg-g00459', 'forest-governance', 'professional-ethics', 'Hard', 'practice',
   'In terms of professional ethics, what is the recommended approach for a forester when new scientific research challenges existing forest management practices?',
   '[{"id":"a","text":"Dismiss the new research in favor of established practices."},{"id":"b","text":"Integrate the new research into current practices after thorough evaluation and peer review."},{"id":"c","text":"Implement changes immediately without further consultation."},{"id":"d","text":"Wait for policy updates before considering any changes."}]'::jsonb, 'b'),
  ('fg-g00460', 'forest-governance', 'professional-ethics', 'Hard', 'practice',
   'What is an ethically appropriate response for a forester when encountering unintentional harm to wildlife during forestry operations?',
   '[{"id":"a","text":"Continue operations as the harm was unintentional."},{"id":"b","text":"Minimize the importance of the incident to stakeholders."},{"id":"c","text":"Report the incident and propose measures to prevent future occurrences."},{"id":"d","text":"Stop all operations indefinitely until all factors are understood."}]'::jsonb, 'c'),
  ('fg-g00461', 'forest-governance', 'professional-ethics', 'Hard', 'practice',
   'How should a forester ethically address the challenge of maintaining transparency in reporting when faced with pressure from stakeholders to withhold negative information?',
   '[{"id":"a","text":"Withhold negative information to maintain stakeholder relationships."},{"id":"b","text":"Selectively report data that portrays the project positively."},{"id":"c","text":"Negotiate with stakeholders to agree on which information to report."},{"id":"d","text":"Ensure transparency by reporting all findings, regardless of stakeholder pressure."}]'::jsonb, 'd'),
  ('fg-g00462', 'forest-governance', 'professional-ethics', 'Hard', 'practice',
   'In the practice of professional ethics, how should a forester approach the issue of potential bias when collaborating with a partner organization known for differing views on forest management?',
   '[{"id":"a","text":"Avoid collaboration to prevent potential bias."},{"id":"b","text":"Adopt the partner organization''s views to streamline collaboration."},{"id":"c","text":"Engage in open dialogue to identify and address potential biases from both parties."},{"id":"d","text":"Ignore potential biases and focus solely on project goals."}]'::jsonb, 'c'),
  ('fg-g00463', 'forest-governance', 'professional-ethics', 'Hard', 'practice',
   'In the context of professional ethics, how should a forester handle the integration of traditional knowledge into modern forest management practices?',
   '[{"id":"a","text":"By disregarding traditional knowledge due to lack of scientific validation."},{"id":"b","text":"By ensuring prior informed consent and acknowledging the source of the knowledge."},{"id":"c","text":"By adapting traditional knowledge without consultation to meet modern standards."},{"id":"d","text":"By incorporating traditional knowledge only when it can be monetized."}]'::jsonb, 'b'),
  ('fg-g00464', 'forest-governance', 'professional-ethics', 'Hard', 'practice',
   'How should a professional forester ethically manage conflicts of interest in collaborative research involving multiple stakeholders, including indigenous communities?',
   '[{"id":"a","text":"By prioritizing the interests of the funding organization."},{"id":"b","text":"By maintaining transparency and ensuring all stakeholders have a voice in decision-making."},{"id":"c","text":"By focusing solely on the scientific outcomes, ignoring stakeholder interests."},{"id":"d","text":"By minimizing communication to prevent disagreements."}]'::jsonb, 'b'),
  ('fg-g00465', 'forest-governance', 'professional-ethics', 'Hard', 'practice',
   'Which ethical principle should guide a forester in the dissemination of research findings that could affect public perception of forest management practices?',
   '[{"id":"a","text":"Ensure accessibility and clarity of the information to all relevant parties."},{"id":"b","text":"Prioritize the interests of sponsors over scientific integrity."},{"id":"c","text":"Only share positive findings to maintain a good public image."},{"id":"d","text":"Delay dissemination until it can be financially beneficial."}]'::jsonb, 'a'),
  ('fg-g00466', 'forest-governance', 'professional-ethics', 'Hard', 'practice',
   'How should a forester ethically approach the challenge of balancing timber production with the conservation of biodiversity in a community forest?',
   '[{"id":"a","text":"By prioritizing timber production to maximize economic gain."},{"id":"b","text":"By engaging the community to develop a management plan that addresses both economic and ecological concerns."},{"id":"c","text":"By focusing solely on conservation, regardless of community needs."},{"id":"d","text":"By alternating between years of exclusive production and conservation."}]'::jsonb, 'b'),
  ('fg-g00467', 'forest-governance', 'professional-ethics', 'Hard', 'practice',
   'In professional ethics, what is the appropriate course of action if a forester discovers discrepancies in data reported by a colleague working on a government-funded reforestation project?',
   '[{"id":"a","text":"Confront the colleague privately and insist on correction."},{"id":"b","text":"Report the discrepancies to the project funders without consulting anyone."},{"id":"c","text":"Ignore the discrepancies to maintain workplace harmony."},{"id":"d","text":"Document the discrepancies and discuss them with the project manager or responsible authority to seek a resolution."}]'::jsonb, 'd'),
  ('fg-g00468', 'forest-governance', 'professional-ethics', 'Hard', 'practice',
   'According to professional ethics, how should a forester handle a situation where they are asked to expedite an environmental clearance process for a development project?',
   '[{"id":"a","text":"Expedite the process to build good relationships with the client."},{"id":"b","text":"Adhere strictly to all legal and procedural requirements despite external pressures."},{"id":"c","text":"Give preferential treatment to projects with substantial financial backing."},{"id":"d","text":"Use discretion to expedite based on personal judgment of project merits."}]'::jsonb, 'b'),
  ('fg-g00469', 'forest-governance', 'professional-ethics', 'Hard', 'practice',
   'What ethical guideline should a forester follow when managing a team to ensure fair and transparent decision-making processes?',
   '[{"id":"a","text":"Favor team members who align with personal viewpoints."},{"id":"b","text":"Encourage diverse perspectives and make decisions based on a consensus or the best available evidence."},{"id":"c","text":"Rely on hierarchical authority to expedite decision-making."},{"id":"d","text":"Limit discussions to avoid potential conflicts."}]'::jsonb, 'b'),
  ('fg-g00470', 'forest-governance', 'professional-ethics', 'Hard', 'practice',
   'In terms of professional ethics, how should a forester deal with the unauthorized use of forest resources by local communities?',
   '[{"id":"a","text":"Immediately report the activities to law enforcement without engaging the community."},{"id":"b","text":"Ignore the activities to maintain good relations with the community."},{"id":"c","text":"Impose penalties without considering the socio-economic context."},{"id":"d","text":"Collaborate with the community to understand their needs and work towards a sustainable solution."}]'::jsonb, 'd'),
  ('fg-g00471', 'forest-governance', 'professional-ethics', 'Hard', 'practice',
   'Which ethical consideration should guide a forester in conducting environmental impact assessments for a new infrastructure project?',
   '[{"id":"a","text":"Ensure comprehensive assessments that consider long-term environmental impacts and involve all stakeholders."},{"id":"b","text":"Focus on minimizing project costs over environmental protection."},{"id":"c","text":"Limit assessments to areas directly affected by construction."},{"id":"d","text":"Prioritize speed and efficiency in completing the assessment."}]'::jsonb, 'a'),
  ('fg-g00472', 'forest-governance', 'professional-ethics', 'Hard', 'practice',
   'How should a forester ethically address the challenge of ensuring fair access to forest resources for marginalized groups within a community?',
   '[{"id":"a","text":"Allow resource distribution based on historical usage patterns only."},{"id":"b","text":"Work with community leaders to develop an inclusive access plan that considers the needs of marginalized groups."},{"id":"c","text":"Focus resource allocation on the economically influential groups to foster development."},{"id":"d","text":"Distribute resources equally among all community members regardless of needs."}]'::jsonb, 'b'),
  ('fg-g00473', 'forest-governance', 'professional-ethics', 'Hard', 'practice',
   'According to the Code of Ethics for Filipino Foresters, which ethical principle is emphasized when a forester is required to make a decision that involves the potential compromise of their professional integrity due to pressure from political actors or corporate entities?',
   '[{"id":"a","text":"Transparency and accountability in all actions and decisions."},{"id":"b","text":"Prioritizing economic benefits over environmental concerns."},{"id":"c","text":"Compromise and negotiation to align with the interests of influential stakeholders."},{"id":"d","text":"Maintaining professional independence and resisting undue influence."}]'::jsonb, 'd'),
  ('fu-g00001', 'forest-utilization', 'wood-structure-identification', 'Easy', 'practice',
   'Which part of the tree is primarily responsible for water and nutrient transport?',
   '[{"id":"a","text":"Heartwood"},{"id":"b","text":"Bark"},{"id":"c","text":"Pith"},{"id":"d","text":"Sapwood"}]'::jsonb, 'd'),
  ('fu-g00002', 'forest-utilization', 'wood-structure-identification', 'Easy', 'practice',
   'What is the primary function of the phloem in a tree?',
   '[{"id":"a","text":"Transport nutrients from the leaves to other parts of the tree"},{"id":"b","text":"Provide structural support"},{"id":"c","text":"Store energy as starch"},{"id":"d","text":"Conduct water and minerals from the roots"}]'::jsonb, 'a'),
  ('fu-g00003', 'forest-utilization', 'wood-structure-identification', 'Easy', 'practice',
   'Which type of cell is primarily responsible for the mechanical support in wood?',
   '[{"id":"a","text":"Tracheids"},{"id":"b","text":"Fibers"},{"id":"c","text":"Parenchyma cells"},{"id":"d","text":"Vessel elements"}]'::jsonb, 'b'),
  ('fu-g00004', 'forest-utilization', 'wood-structure-identification', 'Easy', 'practice',
   'The growth rings visible in a cross-section of a tree trunk are formed by which process?',
   '[{"id":"a","text":"Secondary growth"},{"id":"b","text":"Primary growth"},{"id":"c","text":"Photosynthesis"},{"id":"d","text":"Respiration"}]'::jsonb, 'a'),
  ('fu-g00005', 'forest-utilization', 'wood-structure-identification', 'Easy', 'practice',
   'Which component of wood is primarily responsible for its compression strength?',
   '[{"id":"a","text":"Lignin"},{"id":"b","text":"Cellulose"},{"id":"c","text":"Hemicellulose"},{"id":"d","text":"Pectin"}]'::jsonb, 'a'),
  ('fu-g00006', 'forest-utilization', 'wood-structure-identification', 'Easy', 'practice',
   'Which part of a tree is directly involved in the production of new xylem and phloem?',
   '[{"id":"a","text":"Heartwood"},{"id":"b","text":"Cambium"},{"id":"c","text":"Sapwood"},{"id":"d","text":"Cork"}]'::jsonb, 'b'),
  ('fu-g00007', 'forest-utilization', 'wood-structure-identification', 'Easy', 'practice',
   'The presence of which substance gives heartwood its darker color compared to sapwood?',
   '[{"id":"a","text":"Tannins"},{"id":"b","text":"Chlorophyll"},{"id":"c","text":"Lignin"},{"id":"d","text":"Extractives"}]'::jsonb, 'd'),
  ('fu-g00008', 'forest-utilization', 'wood-structure-identification', 'Easy', 'practice',
   'In wood anatomy, what is the function of ray cells?',
   '[{"id":"a","text":"Provide vertical support"},{"id":"b","text":"Transport nutrients horizontally"},{"id":"c","text":"Store starch"},{"id":"d","text":"Transport water vertically"}]'::jsonb, 'b'),
  ('fu-g00009', 'forest-utilization', 'wood-structure-identification', 'Easy', 'practice',
   'The term ''annual ring'' in wood structure refers to:',
   '[{"id":"a","text":"The growth layer of wood formed in one year"},{"id":"b","text":"The age of the tree in months"},{"id":"c","text":"The cell wall thickness of the wood"},{"id":"d","text":"The average diameter of a tree"}]'::jsonb, 'a'),
  ('fu-g00010', 'forest-utilization', 'wood-structure-identification', 'Easy', 'practice',
   'Which type of wood cell is more abundant in hardwoods compared to softwoods?',
   '[{"id":"a","text":"Tracheids"},{"id":"b","text":"Parenchyma cells"},{"id":"c","text":"Fibers"},{"id":"d","text":"Vessel elements"}]'::jsonb, 'd'),
  ('fu-g00011', 'forest-utilization', 'wood-structure-identification', 'Easy', 'practice',
   'Which wood anatomical feature is primarily used to differentiate between softwoods and hardwoods?',
   '[{"id":"a","text":"Presence of vessels"},{"id":"b","text":"Color variation"},{"id":"c","text":"Moisture content"},{"id":"d","text":"Density differences"}]'::jsonb, 'a'),
  ('fu-g00012', 'forest-utilization', 'wood-structure-identification', 'Easy', 'practice',
   'In wood anatomy, what are the longitudinal cells that primarily conduct water in softwoods called?',
   '[{"id":"a","text":"Vessels"},{"id":"b","text":"Fibers"},{"id":"c","text":"Parenchyma cells"},{"id":"d","text":"Tracheids"}]'::jsonb, 'd'),
  ('fu-g00013', 'forest-utilization', 'wood-structure-identification', 'Easy', 'practice',
   'Which term refers to the small, pore-like structures found in the wood of hardwoods, responsible for water conduction?',
   '[{"id":"a","text":"Vessels"},{"id":"b","text":"Fibers"},{"id":"c","text":"Tracheids"},{"id":"d","text":"Rays"}]'::jsonb, 'a'),
  ('fu-g00014', 'forest-utilization', 'wood-structure-identification', 'Easy', 'practice',
   'What is the name of the wood layer that is responsible for transporting nutrients in a tree?',
   '[{"id":"a","text":"Cambium"},{"id":"b","text":"Phloem"},{"id":"c","text":"Xylem"},{"id":"d","text":"Pith"}]'::jsonb, 'b'),
  ('fu-g00015', 'forest-utilization', 'wood-structure-identification', 'Easy', 'practice',
   'In which part of the tree is the cambium located?',
   '[{"id":"a","text":"Inside the pith"},{"id":"b","text":"On the outer bark"},{"id":"c","text":"Between the xylem and phloem"},{"id":"d","text":"Within the sapwood"}]'::jsonb, 'c'),
  ('fu-g00016', 'forest-utilization', 'wood-structure-identification', 'Easy', 'practice',
   'What is the primary structural component found in the cell walls of wood?',
   '[{"id":"a","text":"Lignin"},{"id":"b","text":"Hemicellulose"},{"id":"c","text":"Cellulose"},{"id":"d","text":"Starch"}]'::jsonb, 'c'),
  ('fu-g00017', 'forest-utilization', 'wood-structure-identification', 'Easy', 'practice',
   'In wood identification, what are rays responsible for?',
   '[{"id":"a","text":"Storing and transporting nutrients laterally"},{"id":"b","text":"Transporting water vertically"},{"id":"c","text":"Providing structural support"},{"id":"d","text":"Resisting microbial attack"}]'::jsonb, 'a'),
  ('fu-g00018', 'forest-utilization', 'wood-structure-identification', 'Easy', 'practice',
   'Which feature is typically used to determine the age of a tree from a cross-section of its trunk?',
   '[{"id":"a","text":"Annual growth rings"},{"id":"b","text":"Vessel arrangement"},{"id":"c","text":"Color of the heartwood"},{"id":"d","text":"Density of the sapwood"}]'::jsonb, 'a'),
  ('fu-g00019', 'forest-utilization', 'wood-structure-identification', 'Easy', 'practice',
   'What is the main role of lignin in wood structure?',
   '[{"id":"a","text":"To conduct water"},{"id":"b","text":"To bind fibers and provide rigidity"},{"id":"c","text":"To provide flexibility"},{"id":"d","text":"To store nutrients"}]'::jsonb, 'b'),
  ('fu-g00020', 'forest-utilization', 'wood-structure-identification', 'Easy', 'practice',
   'Which layer of cells in a tree is responsible for secondary growth, increasing the girth of the tree?',
   '[{"id":"a","text":"Cambium"},{"id":"b","text":"Pith"},{"id":"c","text":"Phloem"},{"id":"d","text":"Xylem"}]'::jsonb, 'a'),
  ('fu-g00021', 'forest-utilization', 'wood-structure-identification', 'Easy', 'practice',
   'What is the primary role of cellulose in wood structure?',
   '[{"id":"a","text":"Transport nutrients and water."},{"id":"b","text":"Protect against insect infestation."},{"id":"c","text":"Provide mechanical strength and rigidity."},{"id":"d","text":"Store energy for the tree."}]'::jsonb, 'c'),
  ('fu-g00022', 'forest-utilization', 'wood-structure-identification', 'Easy', 'practice',
   'In wood anatomy, which type of cells are primarily responsible for water transport in hardwoods?',
   '[{"id":"a","text":"Tracheids."},{"id":"b","text":"Vessels."},{"id":"c","text":"Ray cells."},{"id":"d","text":"Parenchyma cells."}]'::jsonb, 'b'),
  ('fu-g00023', 'forest-utilization', 'wood-structure-identification', 'Easy', 'practice',
   'Which part of the tree trunk is the outermost layer responsible for protection against external damage?',
   '[{"id":"a","text":"Cambium."},{"id":"b","text":"Sapwood."},{"id":"c","text":"Phloem."},{"id":"d","text":"Bark."}]'::jsonb, 'd'),
  ('fu-g00024', 'forest-utilization', 'wood-structure-identification', 'Easy', 'practice',
   'What is the main function of lignin in the cell walls of wood?',
   '[{"id":"a","text":"Conduct water and nutrients."},{"id":"b","text":"Provide rigidity and resistance to decay."},{"id":"c","text":"Store energy and nutrients."},{"id":"d","text":"Facilitate cell division and growth."}]'::jsonb, 'b'),
  ('fu-g00025', 'forest-utilization', 'wood-structure-identification', 'Easy', 'practice',
